// A diagnostic whose two labels sit in different files. The parameter is in
// `other`, the argument is here, and both are shown.
//
// Which came first was decided by comparing the two spans, and a span is a
// byte offset into the file that produced it -- so the order depended on how
// long the other file happened to be, and a comment added there flipped it.
// Ordering is the renderer's: it holds the file table, so it is the only place
// that can compare two positions in different files at all.
//
// It is also the only place that can say which file a line came from, which is
// what `:::` does below. Two files' line 2 stacked with nothing between them
// are two places a reader cannot tell apart.
import other

fn main() -> UInt8 {
    other.f(7)
}
